<title>UK: Byblos Bank sets $50 mln three-year bond, +285 bp.</title>
<headline>Byblos Bank sets $50 mln three-year bond, +285 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Lebanon Invest and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BYBLOS BANK SAL</p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 COUPON     9.25	MATURITY    23.SEP.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.782    PAY DATE    23.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.00	REOFFER    99.782    SPREAD	+285 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  LEBANON   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  0.50	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND THREE-YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
